# SHA-256 (64 lowercase hex chars) of your 12-character gap-library passphrase.
# Rules: exactly 12 characters; include at least one digit and one symbol (non-letter, non-digit).
# Generate locally (do not commit the raw passphrase):
#   node -e "const c=require('crypto');const p='YOUR12CHARS!';if(p.length!==12)throw new Error('length');console.log(c.createHash('sha256').update(p).digest('hex'))"
#
# Copy the printed hex into .env.local as:
#   VITE_GAP_UNLOCK_SHA256=paste_hex_here
#
# Alternatively, paste the same hex into src/config/gapLockSecret.js as GAP_UNLOCK_SHA256_FALLBACK.
#
# If unset, gap articles (slugs A##-*, B##-*, D##-*, E##-*) stay off the home page and
# direct URLs show a lock screen until unlock is configured and the passphrase is entered
# at /unlock-gaps in the browser.
#
# Copy to a gitignored file and fill in the hex:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# (.env, .env.* except .env.example, and *.local are ignored by git.)

# VITE_GAP_UNLOCK_SHA256=
